course: dictionary
lesson: 14344
title: Odourless: no smell at all
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Odourless means having no smell at all. The word is built from odour, which means smell, and -less, which means without. So odourless means without any smell.
explain: Odourless is not the same as smelly or sweet-smelling. «The water in the glass was colourless and odourless.» You could look at it and sniff it, and your nose would find nothing.
explain: Scientists use this word a lot. Pure water is odourless, and so are gases such as oxygen. Some dangerous gases are odourless too, so you cannot smell them coming. That is why we need alarms.
fact: Odourless means having no smell at all.
fact: The American spelling is odorless, without the u.
fact: «Colourless and odourless» means you cannot see it or smell it.
fact: Carbon monoxide is an odourless gas, so you cannot smell it when it is there. That is why alarms are needed.
fact: Natural gas at home has a smell added on purpose, so a leak can be noticed.
exercise: «The water in the glass was clear and odourless.» What does odourless mean? | It smells of roses | It is very cold | It is hard to see | *It has no smell at all
exercise: «Carbon monoxide is an odourless gas, so people cannot smell it.» Why do we need alarms for it? | Because it is a sweet food | Because it makes a loud noise | Because it smells very strong | *Because we cannot smell it when it is there
exercise: Which spelling is the American one for odourless? | odourful | colourless | odour | *odorless
test: «The natural gas in our kitchen has a smell added, because the gas itself is odourless.» Why is the smell added? | To make the gas heavier | To make the gas taste sweet | *So a leak can be noticed | To make the kitchen smell nice
test: «The drink was odourless and tasteless.» What does this tell you about the drink? | It is hot and sweet | *It has no smell and no taste | It smells and tastes of lemon | It is very loud
exam: Pure water is odourless. What does this tell you about pure water? | *It has no smell at all, so your nose cannot tell it apart from air | It is always salty | It has no smell | It smells of fruit
